# Derek Rah Peters (bouyonmusique.com, wave 6 parity, 2026-10-20)
# Sources used:
# - Timothy Rommen, Creolite, (Im)Mobility, and Music in Dominica, Journal of Musicology Vol. 32 Issue 4 (opened 2026-10-20 via Academia.edu): Rah (Derrick Peters) was WCK lead singer, principal songwriter and drummer during the band formative years; he joined WCK after the core personnel had been recruited and the band named, by which time Cornell and Keith had decided to modernize Dominica traditional rhythms; his own interview of 24 October 2012 recalls a lapo kabwit drumming corps that made its own drums at carnival time, and following his people in Rosalie, a small village on the Atlantic coast of Dominica, whose quadrille group played jing ping, seen from when he was two years old.
# - Wikipedia and Alchetron, Windward Caribbean Kulture (opened 2026-10-20): WCK formed in 1988 in Roseau, Dominica, credited with creating bouyon in the late 1980s; former members list gives Derick "Rah" Peters, drums and lead vocals; full album discography 1988 to 2011 and hit singles list including Culture Shock 1990, Follow the Leader 1991, Conch Shell/Vola 1993, Balance Batty 1995, Drum Song 1996, Mic Rah Phone 1999.
# - DOM767, Dompedia profile Cornell Fingers Phillip (opened 2026-10-20): in 1988 Phillip and the original members of WCK, including Derek "Rah" Peters and Keith Goddard, sought to create a new sound by blending lapo kabwit drum rhythms, cadence-lypso syncopation and the digital pulse of synthesisers, and created bouyon.
# - DOM767 news, Dominica State College A.C.T.S Summer Camp (published 18 June 2024, opened 2026-10-20): the camp running 15 July to 9 August 2024 for children aged 6 to 15 lists drumming sessions by cultural icon Derek "Rah" Peters during the culture week.
# - Listen Notes, Civic Vibes Program episode Two Trending Topics in Our Culture, live streamed 20 October 2024 (opened 2026-10-20): Mr. Derick "Rah" Peters, billed as the Original Bouyan Pioneer (spelling Bouyan in that listing), discusses the impact of bouyon music on the culture in Dominica in segment 2, after Gregory Rabess in segment 1.
# - Alchetron, Culture of Dominica (opened 2026-10-20): Dominican born Derick "Rah" Peters is considered to be one of the most influential figures in the development of the bouyon genre.
# - Billboard reporting republished by Z89, Inside Bouyon (opened 2026-10-20): WCK formally debuted with One More Sway in 1988, Culture Shock in 1990 housed Dance Floor and the title track, Forever in 1993 and Conch Shell, Tou Cho Tou Flam in 1995 and Balance Batty, tours of the United States, Canada, Europe and the Caribbean, Apollo Theater.
# Spelling note: the sources write his first name three ways: Derek in DOM767, Derick in the WCK member lists and the Civic Vibes listing, Derrick in Rommen academic article and in Culture of Dominica. This profile uses Derek, the spelling carried by DOM767 and by this page slug, and flags the variants openly in the text and the FAQ. No official artist page was opened and verified during this research, so sameAs stays empty.

